{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "book-route-qualification-record",
  "route": {
    "id": "psionic-public-models",
    "book": "psionic",
    "title": "Train and resume a tiny module, then inspect MLP and CNN models",
    "scope": "Actually train the existing 76-parameter public module for 400 tiny SGD steps, compare every loss and saved float with its reference loop, and resume from step 200. Then construct the public 3322-parameter MLP and 2910-parameter CNN, execute synthetic zero-model gradients and demonstrate atomic refusal of unrepresentable compute weights.",
    "limitations": [
      "Only the tiny fixed module is trained here. The MLP and CNN steps are dataset-free API/refusal examples and do not rerun the frozen MNIST learning experiments.",
      "Retained MLP/CNN quality, independent gradients, replay and export records remain separate. Exact example output does not requalify those experiments on this compiler or host.",
      "Convolution is CPU f32 NCHW/OIHW valid stride one with formal first-order f64 tape derivatives. GPU convolution, compiled convolution backward, higher-order transforms, pooling and broader architecture acceptance remain outside this route.",
      "Examples do not count as product adoption. The native mnist-experiment.coax and cnn-experiment.coax consumers retain separate workload and quality gates."
    ]
  },
